(1. Introduction & Overview) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(The Software Development Life Cycle \(SDLC\) is a structured framework that guides) Tj
0 -13 Td
(the conception, specification, development, verification, deployment, and) Tj
0 -13 Td
(operational maintenance of reliable software systems. By enforcing defined) Tj
0 -13 Td
(milestones and quality gates between phases, SDLC disciplines prevent runaway) Tj
0 -13 Td
(defect costs and align engineering outputs with institutional and stakeholder) Tj
0 -13 Td
(requirements.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
0 -24 Td
(2. Core Architectural Phases) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(A standard software engineering lifecycle comprises five core stages:) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Requirement Analysis: Eliciting user needs, evaluating operational constraints,) Tj
0 -13 Td
(and drafting unambiguous Functional & Non-Functional Specifications.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Architectural Design: Structuring multi-tier architectures, data schemas,) Tj
0 -13 Td
(module cohesion, interface contracts, and component decoupling.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Implementation: Coding clean, documented, and modular routines adhering to) Tj
0 -13 Td
(established language guidelines and peer review standards.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Verification & Testing: Subjecting software to unit, integration, system, and) Tj
0 -13 Td
(user acceptance test suites to detect regressions before release.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Evolution & Maintenance: Addressing post-deployment defects, adapting to) Tj
0 -13 Td
(updated operational runtime environments, and enhancing capabilities.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
0 -24 Td
(3. The Defect Amplification Model \(Boehm's Law\)) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Empirical studies demonstrate that defect remediation costs increase) Tj
0 -13 Td
(exponentially across successive SDLC phases. A requirement ambiguity resolved) Tj
0 -13 Td
(during initial analysis costs approximately 1x to fix. The same defect discovered) Tj
0 -13 Td
(during coding costs 5x, during integration testing costs 10x, and post-deployment) Tj
0 -13 Td
(in production exceeds 30x to 100x. Systematic upstream verification is therefore) Tj
0 -13 Td
(essential.) Tj
/F2 12 Tf
0 -24 Td
(4. Multi-Tier Operational Environments) Tj
/F1 9 Tf
0 -13 Td
(Enterprise deployment mandates strict physical or logical separation between) Tj
0 -13 Td
(operational environments:) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Development \(Dev\): Dynamic, unstable staging environment for rapid prototyping) Tj
0 -13 Td
(and unit testing.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Quality Assurance \(QA\): Isolated replica of production infrastructure executing) Tj
0 -13 Td
(automated regression suites, load testing, and UAT sign-offs.) Tj
0 -13 Td
(? Production \(Prod\): Live, monitored environment delivering services to) Tj
0 -13 Td
(authenticated end users under rigorous change control.) Tj
